@* Mobile-only quick access to the three screens used most. Everything else — add recipe,
   settings, admin — stays in the drawer behind the hamburger, so this bar never needs to
   grow or change by role. Hidden from the shell breakpoint up, where the sidebar is
   permanently on screen and this would just repeat it.

   Rendered by MainLayout, which is the authenticated layout, so there is no role or
   sign-in check here: every destination is open to any logged-in user. *@

<nav class="fh-bottom-nav" aria-label="@UiText.Layout.QuickNavigation">
	@* Match.All on /recipes so browsing does not stay highlighted while you are on
	   /recipes/find or /recipes/create, which are prefixes of it. *@
	<NavLink class="fh-bottom-nav__item" href="/recipes" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">
		<i class="bi bi-journal-text" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		<span>@UiText.Nav.Recipes</span>
	</NavLink>
	<NavLink class="fh-bottom-nav__item" href="/recipes/find">
		<i class="bi bi-search-heart" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		<span>@UiText.Nav.FindRecipesShort</span>
	</NavLink>
	<NavLink class="fh-bottom-nav__item" href="/calendar">
		<i class="bi bi-calendar-week" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		<span>@UiText.Nav.Calendar</span>
	</NavLink>
</nav>
